- [ ] Add a `.gitignore`: `db/`, `*.wav`, `*.als`, `__pycache__/`, `.env`
- [ ] Write `CLAUDE.md` with: "Explain all audio jargon in plain English. Never assume producer vocabulary. This repo controls Ableton Live 12 on Windows."

### 0.3 Install Producer Pal (the stable core)

- [ ] Download the `.amxd` device + `.mcpb` extension from producer-pal.org
- [ ] Double-click `.mcpb` → installs into Claude Desktop
- [ ] Drop `Producer_Pal.amxd` on an empty MIDI track named `PP`
- [ ] Save that track into your default template (File → Save Live Set as Default)
- [ ] Test in Claude Desktop: "connect to my Live set and tell me the tempo"

**Why keep Producer Pal when we're building our own?** It's the reliable fallback while the custom server is under construction, and its Agent Skill/REST API are reference implementations to learn from. Retire it later if the custom build fully surpasses it.

