## Phase 3 — The Knowledge: Plugin Dictionary + Macro Racks (ongoing)

**Rule: document plugins the day you first reach for them, not all upfront.** Seed with the workhorses.

### 3.1 Dictionary template (`plugin-dictionary/_TEMPLATE.md`)

```markdown
# [Plugin Name]
**What it is (plain English):**
**When we reach for it:**
**Key controls:** (name → what it does, in human words)
**Macro rack:** AGT [name] — knob list with names
**Agent access:** macro rack / direct params (see .params.json) / manual only
**Gotchas:**
**Recipes that use it:** (links into /skills)
```

### 3.2 Macro racks (the AGT presets)

→ *A rack wraps a plugin and forwards its most important controls to up to 16 named knobs the agent can read and drive.*

- [ ] Build and save to User Library, prefix `AGT `:
  - [ ] `AGT Serum2` — Cutoff, Resonance, Wave Position, Unison Detune, Drive, LFO Rate, FX Mix, Space
  - [ ] `AGT ProC2` — Threshold, Ratio, Attack, Release, Makeup, Dry/Wet
  - [ ] `AGT Saturn2` — Drive, Mix, Tone
  - [ ] `AGT Decapitator` — Drive, Mix, Tone, Style
  - [ ] `AGT AlterBoy` — Pitch, Formant, Drive, Mix
  - [ ] `AGT KClip` — Input Drive, Output Trim, Mix
- [ ] Pro-Q 4 and Pro-L: **no rack** — dictionary entries marked "agent sets directly" (precision EQ moves and limiter gain work better as direct parameter calls)
- [ ] Run `param_dump` on each plugin as you rack it; save the JSON next to its dictionary page

